WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:04.036
HOST: Kelly, Justin,
congratulations, you've

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:05.471
made it to the final round.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.339
Which means you're both one
step closer to the title

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:09.942
of "Forged in Fire"
champion and receiving

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:11.377
that check for 10 grand.

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:13.379
Now we're sending you back
to your home forges where

00:00:13.445 --> 00:00:15.781
we're asking you to
forge an iconic weapon

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:19.753
from history, the falcata.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:26.191
The falcata is a curved chopping
weapon with a sharpened point.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.127
It was popular in
pre-Roman Iberia

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.063
in what is now
Spain and Portugal.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.699
It is unknown whether the
weapon was created in Iberia

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:35.768
or evolved from designs in
central Europe in Greece.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:40.273
Whatever its origins, it earned
its reputation as a killer.

00:00:40.339 --> 00:00:42.542
Employed by Spanish
infantry, that falcata

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:45.945
allowed its user to deliver a
blow with the force of an ax

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.514
while cutting like a sword.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.383
Hannibal of Carthage was so
impressed by this Spanish blade

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.718
that he equipped many of
his African troops with it.

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:56.155
Those armed with a falcata
would rely on speed and agility

00:00:56.221 --> 00:00:59.559
against the heavily
armored Roman soldiers.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.795
Bladesmiths, you will have
five days to accomplish this.

00:01:02.861 --> 00:01:05.531
At the end of those five days
you will return and present

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:07.200
your finished
falcatas to our panel

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.002
of expert judges, who will
then submit them to a series

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.271
of very rigorous tests.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.872
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:16.742
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:23.049 line:7%
[music playing]

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:25.885
 Here we are at my home
forge where I'm very comfy.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:26.852
I love it here.

00:01:26.952 --> 00:01:28.555
I have an awesome set of tools.

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.723
I know what glue is what.

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:31.491
I'm ready to roll.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.161
I'm real comfortable
building a facata.

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:37.730
I like that shape of blade.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.232
Probably the most
challenging part

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.935
is gonna be to decorate it
to where it really pops out.

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.336
I've decided since I am
a farrier that I should

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:45.871
probably go for the
decorative horse

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:48.140
heads on the end of the handle.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.209
I'm taking a fair
amount of time to try

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:52.579
to get the look of this
horse down because, you know,

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:53.713
I want the perfect horse.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.648
And I want the horse that
goes with that knife.

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:01.955
Very important to know
your horse anatomy.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:05.524
He looks like he's about
a big hunk out of you.

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:06.992
It's going be a lot
of work but I want

00:02:07.092 --> 00:02:08.928
to hand in the coolest project.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:12.265
And I want something
that's true to the era,

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:13.800
but it's got a little
Kelly in it too.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.873
[music playing]

00:02:20.939 --> 00:02:24.277
 I'm excited to be back home
with tools I'm familiar with,

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:25.812
but I have a big
challenge ahead of me

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:29.448
and some really
tough competition.

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:34.186
Today, I'd like to design
the blade and start forging.

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:36.522
I'm not a swordsmith,
I'm a bladesmith.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:40.126
The falcata is a large sword,
but a big part of bladesmithing

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.494
is problem-solving.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:44.430 line:0%
I'm going to be
using leaf spring.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:47.433 line:0%
It's very thick,
it's very heavy.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:52.972
It's the end of day one, what
I have is a pointy metal stick.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.106
Tomorrow's going
to be a long day.

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.709 line:7%
[music playing]

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:03.849
 Day three, I'm feeling
really good about the progress.

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:05.317
Looking fine to me.

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:06.953
The heat treat went really well.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.055
Everything's nice
and straight so it's

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:11.557
just chugging right along.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.426
Just going to tighten up
the handle a little bit.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:18.330
Historically, it kind of wraps
around and protects your hand.

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:20.299
I cut out a V and it's
mild steel right there,

00:03:20.365 --> 00:03:21.901
so I'm just going to
take a little hand torch

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.402
and heat this up a little bit.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.704
Just bend around, reweld it.

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.711
So I like the shape
of it better now.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:33.011
It welded up nice.

00:03:33.078 --> 00:03:34.781
You can't really see a seam.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.082 line:7%
I like it.

00:03:37.182 --> 00:03:38.685 line:7%
 It's my last day.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.920 line:0%
I need to get a finish on this
blade, glue up the handles,

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.254
and then sharpen it.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.290
Making a blade
this big with just

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:46.859
the tools I have at my
disposal is a lot of work.

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:49.963
But I think I did as good
a job as anybody could do,

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.797
and I feel this is
a winning weapon.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.866
Falcata!

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:55.301
I think Kelly should be worried.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.802
She's going to have to bring
a blade that can perform

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.904
just as well, or better.

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:00.306
Cool.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.608
And that's quite a challenge
for anybody I believe.

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:05.244
JUDGE: Bladesmiths, to see
how sharp your blades are,

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.312
I will take your weapon,
and I will see how well

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:09.915
it does against these fish.

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:10.883
Kelly you're up first.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:11.650
You ready?

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:12.852
 Yep.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.755
Going into the testing, I'm
just glad when it's over

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:18.690
and I'll be back to normal
Kelly not stressed-out Kelly.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.659
Because I'm much more fun
when I'm normal Kelly.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.029
[music playing]

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:32.070
JUDGE: Well, Kelly,
your blade definitely

00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:34.206
is designed to chop through.

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:36.075
It cut through the first
two fish and almost

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.543
through the third one.

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:39.679
This will cut.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:40.979
Good job.

00:04:41.046 --> 00:04:41.780
Justin, you're up next.

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:42.515
You ready?

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:43.215
 I'm ready.

00:04:43.315 --> 00:04:45.051
JUDGE: Let's do this.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:47.753
JUSTIN: Watching Kelly's blade
go through 2 and 1/2 fish

00:04:47.853 --> 00:04:49.922
set the bar high,
and I have no idea

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:50.956
how this thing will perform.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:53.960
[music playing]

00:04:58.297 --> 00:05:00.732
JUDGE: Well, Justin,
your blade is sharp.

00:05:00.799 --> 00:05:03.036
It cut all the way through
the first and second

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.737
and into the third.

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.071
It'll cut.

00:05:06.171 --> 00:05:08.140
Next stop is a strength test.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.809
Dave?

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:13.479
Smiths, on the battlefield the
falcata didn't only hit skin,

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:16.582
it hit other swords,
armor, and shields.

00:05:16.648 --> 00:05:18.384
So to test the
strength of your blade,

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.486
we're going to use
our device here

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:24.222
to take three blows into the
steel edge of this shield.

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:25.491
If your blades
are made properly,

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.293
that edge should hold up.

00:05:27.359 --> 00:05:29.862
If not, we'll see what happens.

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:30.997
Kelly you're up first.

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:32.164
You ready?

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:32.832
 Sure.

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.200
OK.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.435
 I'm a little nervous
about the strength test.

00:05:36.535 --> 00:05:40.005
Don't be soft piece of
garbage, just be good.

00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:43.743
 In 3, 2, 1.

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.451
3, 2, 1.

00:05:58.091 --> 00:05:59.558
I thought I was
seeing the crack,

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.827
but it's just discoloration.

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:05.597
The edge held up beautifully,
it's still sharp.

00:06:05.697 --> 00:06:09.101
All in all, held up beautifully
in the strength test.

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:10.035
Justin, you ready?

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:10.869
 I'm ready.

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:12.104
 All right.

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:14.306
 I feel like this final
test is really going to show

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:15.508
what my blade's made of.

00:06:15.574 --> 00:06:16.842
Either it's going
to hold together,

00:06:16.942 --> 00:06:19.311
it's going to perform well,
or it may break in half.

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.145
I have no idea.

00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:22.882
 3, 2, 1.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:28.220
All right, last time.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:30.156
3, 2, 1.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:38.631
Well, I'm impressed.

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:43.770
No deformation, it's
still sharp, nicely done.

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:46.672
But that's scary.

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:47.973
Very scary.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.743
It's in a position that if
blade rotates one direction,

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.511
it's going to go right
into the pad of the thumb.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.780
It rotates the other
direction, it's

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:57.082
going to cut into the tendons
in the back of the hand.

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:58.350
That's an issue.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:01.988
But all in all, it did
well in the machine.

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:02.788
Good job.

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:05.258
 Thank you.

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:07.360
HOST: Kelly, Justin.

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:09.529
Before I announce the
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:12.231
the judges have something they'd
like to say to both of you.

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:13.131
Jason?

00:07:13.198 --> 00:07:14.533
 Kelly.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:15.600
One of the things that
I appreciate the most

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.336 line:0%
is how you forged
the horse head.

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:18.904 line:7%
I like the way it looked.

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:22.174 line:0%
Also, it's traditional for a
falcata to have a horse head.

00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:23.942
Overall it was a
beautiful piece.

00:07:24.042 --> 00:07:24.710
 Thank you.

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:25.711
 Very nice.

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:26.745
HOST: Dave?

00:07:26.845 --> 00:07:29.148
 Justin, you came up
with a design there

00:07:29.214 --> 00:07:32.117
that is a complete intimidator.

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:34.620 line:0%
I mean, you look at that thing
and you know it's going to hurt

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.222 line:7%
you if it gets close to you.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:37.890 line:0%
Really appreciate your
bringing something

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:39.992
that is solidly yours.

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:42.127
 Means a lot, thank you.

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:46.566
 Kelly, Justin, you've both
done very impressive work.

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:50.269
However, on this day, there can
only be one "Forged in Fire"

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:51.002
champion.

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:57.576
[music playing]

00:07:57.643 --> 00:07:58.911
 Kelly, congratulations.

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:00.278
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:03.215
[music playing]

00:08:03.315 --> 00:08:06.752
HOST: Justin, unfortunately
your blade did not make the cut.

00:08:06.852 --> 00:08:09.589
JUDGE: Justin, the handle is
a connection between the end

00:08:09.689 --> 00:08:11.056
user and the blade.

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:13.926 line:0%
Your handle construction,
with that hook being sharp,

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:16.462 line:0%
you could potentially hurt
the person wielding it,

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:18.397
which, unfortunately,
prevents it from being

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:20.399
a fully functional weapon.

00:08:20.499 --> 00:08:22.334
And it's for that
reason that your blade

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:23.568
did not make the cut.

00:08:23.668 --> 00:08:27.439
HOST: Justin, please
surrender your weapon.

00:08:27.506 --> 00:08:28.841
 It was close.

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:30.843
It's nice to know that
with five days of hard work

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:33.712
I can impress the judges
that have seen many swords.

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.313
And I've competed
with some of the best

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:36.548
bladesmiths in the country.

00:08:36.648 --> 00:08:40.152
To do that is really rewarding.

00:08:40.252 --> 00:08:41.420
HOST: Kelly, congratulations.

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:42.954
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:08:43.021 --> 00:08:46.025
You will also be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:08:46.125 --> 00:08:46.959
How does that make you feel?

00:08:47.026 --> 00:08:47.760
 Feels great.

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:52.131
DAVE: I think that
thing is great.

00:08:52.198 --> 00:08:54.600
It's straight up right
out of the history books.

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:56.301
I mean, it's got all the
elements, which is really

00:08:56.401 --> 00:08:57.703
neat, including the horse head.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.838
HOST: It's awesome, your
our first female champion.

00:08:59.905 --> 00:09:02.007
 No, it just still
didn't seem quite real.

00:09:02.074 --> 00:09:04.309
It feels great to be the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.911
The first ferrier
"Forged in Fire"

00:09:06.011 --> 00:09:09.214
champion, the first chick
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:09.281 --> 00:09:10.382
That's pretty cool.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:11.217
I pulled it off.

00:09:11.284 --> 00:09:14.220
[music playing]

